;;; conjurer.cnj
;;; The charter of the Conjurer language itself.
;;;
;;; The specification argues that intent is the source and every artefact a
;;; build of it. This file applies that to the specification: the reasons for
;;; the language's shape live here, not only in the CHANGELOG, the proposals
;;; and the conversations in which they were decided.
;;;
;;; Decisions taken before 2026-10-13 were recovered, not authored here. Each
;;; carries :recovered with its grade and :source with the record it was read
;;; from, as x/charter would emit them. Where the why was never written down,
;;; it is an :open question rather than a reason supplied after the fact.

;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;; Section 1 — Charter
;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(charter "Conjurer"
  :version  "0.1.0"
  :created  "2026-10-13"
  :updated  "2026-10-13"
  :domain   "Conjurer, a declarative language for working with LLMs: its
             philosophy (conjurer.md), the twelve standard grimoires, the
             template for grimoires and .cnj files, the symbol catalogue
             (index.edn), the entry documents for processors and readers, and
             the worked examples."
  :language :en

  :goals [
    "Keep intent as the source: a .cnj file is the durable statement of what
     should exist, and code is a build that can be regenerated, retargeted or
     discarded."
    "Say honestly what is deterministic and what is semantic: every binding
     statement can be traced to the layer that holds it, and nothing claims a
     layer it cannot reach."
    "Make uncertainty part of the language: how well something is known is
     graded, and a guess is never presented as a fact."
    "Run the flow both ways: intent manifests forward into artefacts, and
     artefacts are exhumed back into intent."
    "Stay small and coherent: grow the language from real use, keep its form
     symmetric, and prefer the elegant solution to the complete one."]

  :audience {:primary   :maintainer
             :secondary [:practitioner :llm-processor :tool-builder]}

  :decisions [

    ;; ── Recovered: repository and baseline ─────────────────────────

    {:id        :clean-grimoire-names
     :date      "2026-05-22"
     :decision  "Grimoire files carry clean names without numeric prefixes
                 (core.md, not 010_core_cnj.md)."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "git: the first scaffolding commit already uses clean names;
                 the maintainer's design notes state the rule as never to be
                 broken"
     :note      "Why is not recorded; see :open."}

    {:id        :determinism-boundary
     :date      "2026-06-05"
     :decision  "Tooling for Conjurer embeds no model. Parsing, validation,
                 references and dependency order are deterministic and belong to
                 a processor such as conjurer-mcp; interpreting meaning belongs to
                 the model in the editor. Reason recorded at the time: a small,
                 testable, fast server without keys or model dependencies."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "examples/conjurer-mcp/conjurer-mcp.cnj, decision of 2026-06-05;
                 architecture.md, The determinism boundary"}

    {:id        :exhume-as-inverse
     :date      "2026-06-06"
     :decision  "The standard library includes exhume, the reverse flow: code is
                 read back into specification, every claim graded attested or
                 inferred."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.0.0"}

    {:id        :changelog-baseline
     :date      "2026-06-06"
     :decision  "The changelog starts at the maturity baseline of 1.0.0; earlier
                 exploratory evolution is pre-history."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md, preamble"}

    {:id        :foresight-grimoire
     :date      "2026-06-10"
     :decision  "Deferred ideas are first-class: foresight records graded
                 candidates, appends reassessments to their :history, and closes
                 them with f/hoist. Abandonment is a status, not an event, so
                 there is no f/abandon."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.1.0; foresight.md, Hoist as an event, abandon as
                 a status"}

    {:id        :materialise-two-phase
     :date      "2026-06-10"
     :decision  "materialise runs a deterministic preflight before semantic
                 generation and halts on unresolved references by default:
                 verify the lossless plan before risking the lossy act."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.1.0; conjurer.md, Symmetry compresses; broken
                 symmetry informs"}

    ;; ── Recovered: the July evaluation ──────────────────────────────

    {:id        :abstraction-layer
     :date      "2026-07-01"
     :decision  "Practitioners name their own patterns: spell, charm and
                 incantation in core, and grimoire for packaging them. :forbids
                 joins the intent topology on conjure, with the force of
                 :requires and the opposite sign."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-07-spec-evaluation.md, Part V"}

    {:id        :verification-stays-layered
     :date      "2026-07-01"
     :decision  "No unified verification grimoire. Verification stays spread
                 over ensure, data/generate-tests, a/evaluate and w/audit,
                 because that scattering is correct layering, not a gap."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-07-spec-evaluation.md, Part V"}

    {:id        :standard-library-freeze
     :date      "2026-07-01"
     :decision  "No further grimoires are under active consideration for the
                 standard library. The scry candidate waits until this freeze is
                 explicitly revisited."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "conjurer.md, The grimoire ecosystem;
                 proposals/2026-07-spec-evaluation.md, Part V"}

    {:id        :no-hardcoded-counts
     :date      "2026-07-01"
     :decision  "Entry documents do not hardcode the symbol count; index.edn is
                 the one place it can be read. A hardcoded count had drifted."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.2.0"}

    {:id        :notes-genre-contract
     :date      "2026-07-04"
     :decision  "Implementation notes for LLM processors follow one contract: a
                 modality scale (must and never bind; prefer and should yield
                 and are surfaced; flag means surface and continue), explicit
                 parameters over notes over examples, and layer attribution for
                 runtime properties."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.2.0; template.md"}

    {:id        :intent-sourced-programming
     :date      "2026-07-08"
     :decision  "The paradigm is named intent-sourced programming: intent is the
                 source, code is the build. Distinguished from Spec-Driven
                 Development, where the specification is consumed once."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.2.0; conjurer.md, What Conjurer is"}

    ;; ── Recovered: the October passes ───────────────────────────────

    {:id        :symmetric-form-shape
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "Every form has the shape (head name :param value ...), with
                 parameters in pairs. The phantom (context establish ...) broke
                 that symmetry and was removed everywhere."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md, Unreleased; template.md, Form shape"}

    {:id        :british-prose-stable-symbols
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "Prose uses British spelling. Symbol names and parameter
                 keywords keep their spelling (e/formalize, w/analyze): renaming
                 a symbol breaks every caller for a spelling preference."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md, Unreleased; proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md,
                 Part IV"}

    {:id        :three-version-lines
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "Three version lines run independently, each with one owner: the
                 specification release (package version, set by release-please
                 and followed by CHANGELOG.md), the catalogue in index.edn, and
                 each grimoire's own version. All follow semantic versioning."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md, Part V (f/hoist
                 :version-model); template.md, Versioning"}

    {:id        :template-owns-cnj-structure
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "template.md Part II is the only place the .cnj structure is
                 defined: nine sections, abstractions and foresight included.
                 core.md and quick-reference.md point to it. Three copies had
                 already drifted once."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md, Part V (f/hoist
                 :cnj-structure-owner)"}

    {:id        :decision-identifiers
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "Charter decisions carry :id when referred to and :supersedes
                 when reversing another; the log is append-only and a reversal is
                 a new entry."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md, Part V (f/hoist
                 :decision-ids)"}

    {:id        :expression-prelude
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "A closed prelude lists the expressions a deterministic processor
                 may evaluate; every other head is a semantic function. The
                 determinism boundary became a property of the language rather
                 than a project rule."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md, Part V (f/hoist
                 :expression-prelude)"}

    {:id        :confidence-two-axes
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "One confidence vocabulary on two axes, provenance and degree; a
                 number only with its basis named."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md, Part V (f/hoist
                 :confidence-vocabulary)"}

    ;; ── Recovered from the maintainer's design notes ────────────────

    {:id        :house-rules
     :date      "2026-10-13"
     :decision  "Recorded as house rules, in force before this charter existed:
                 all canonical specification and design text is in English
                 whatever language the conversation is in, Dutch only where
                 localisation is itself the subject; Mermaid diagrams contain no
                 HTML markup and no emoji; form annotations document only
                 non-obvious external connections, never restate the code; an
                 asset's :conventions are plain prose rather than path
                 templates; elegance and simplicity are the primary design
                 criteria."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "the maintainer's design notes, kept from design conversations"
     :note      "The date is when they were recorded here, not when they were
                 decided; those dates and most of the reasons were not kept.
                 See :open."}

    ;; ── Authored 2026-10-13: Intent over vibes ──────────────────────

    {:id       :self-charter
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "Conjurer keeps its own charter, in design/conjurer.cnj. Its
                history is recovered from the CHANGELOG, the proposals, git and
                the design notes, each entry graded. Reason: the language says
                intent is the source and a decision log prevents re-arguing
                settled questions; it should hold its own reasons the same way.
                Two hoists of 2026-10-12 pointed at :decision/three-version-lines
                and :decision/template-owns-cnj-structure, which existed nowhere
                until now."}

    {:id       :transcripts-as-evidence
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "x/reconstruct-decisions reads session transcripts (:from
                :transcripts, located by :transcripts). A transcript is the one
                trace written while a decision was being made; it is read by
                speaker, so a model's untaken proposal is never recorded as the
                practitioner's decision, and output accepted without comment
                gets a :speculative why. exhume 2.0.0 -> 2.1.0, index.edn 2.0.0 ->
                2.1.0."}

    {:id       :variance-surface
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "core names the variance surface: the binding statements of a
                specification that only the :llm layer will honour. It is read
                off the form, listed by explain :show [:variance-surface], and
                reduced where it matters by writing a predicate in the prelude
                or naming :tests or :lint. Specification side only in this round;
                tool support is :variance-surface-report below. core 3.0.0 ->
                3.1.0."}

    {:id       :crystallisation
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "Conjurer does not forbid exploring by conversation; it absorbs
                it. conjurer.md says so under What Conjurer is not, and exhume
                gains the integration pattern Crystallising an exploratory
                prototype: explore, exhume the model and decisions, charter what
                survived, materialise from a preflight, park the rest in
                foresight, and explore again when a genuine unknown appears.
                Reason: specifying before discovery freezes ignorance, and
                discovering without crystallising loses what was found."}]

  :open [
    "Why were numeric prefixes dropped from the grimoire file names before the
     repository was created? (reason not recorded)"
    "What are the reasons behind the house rules in :decision/house-rules?
     Each should be recorded where it is known; until then they are rules
     without a written why."
    "Should this file be validated by conjurer-mcp in CI, and in which
     validate_cnj mode: authored, or recovered for its history?"
    "Do the live candidates graded in proposals/ (:scry-grimoire,
     :primitive-time-by-parameter, :names-are-symbols) move into Section 8
     of this file, or stay in the evaluation that graded them?"]

  :references ["../examples/conjurer-mcp/conjurer-mcp.cnj"]
  :tags       [:language :specification :meta])

;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;; Section 2 — Assets
;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(asset :grimoire-template
  :type        :code-standard
  :description "The structure every grimoire follows, the form-shape and
                versioning rules, the implementation-notes contract, and the
                one definition of the .cnj file structure."
  :language    :markdown
  :location    "../template.md"
  :enforces    [:canonical-grimoire-structure :form-shape :three-version-lines
                :implementation-notes-contract]
  :applies-to  [:grimoire :cnj-file :entry-document]
  :active-in   :project)

(asset :symbol-catalogue
  :type        :api-specification
  :description "Every symbol across the grimoires with its key parameters, and
                the prelude a deterministic processor may evaluate. The routing
                layer for processors and tools."
  :language    :edn
  :location    "../index.edn"
  :applies-to  [:grimoire :entry-document :tooling]
  :active-in   :project)

;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;; Section 3 — Assumptions
;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(assume
  :environment    :specification-repository
  :team           {:size 1 :skill-level :expert}
  :infrastructure {:existing [:github :release-please :conjurer-mcp]
                   :avoid    [:model-embedded-in-tooling]}
  :non-negotiable [:english-canonical-text :append-only-decisions
                   :graded-recovery :no-fabricated-rationale]
  :negotiable     [:grimoire-count :entry-document-layout])

;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;; Section 8 — Foresight
;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(f/candidate :variance-surface-report
  :label     "conjurer-mcp reports the variance surface of a .cnj file"
  :added     "2026-10-13"
  :status    :proposed
  :scores    {:feasibility 7 :elegance 8 :containment 8 :value 8}
  :rationale "The classification is mechanical — prelude membership,
              :verify-via, and which structural checkers the server offers — so
              a deterministic processor can produce it without generating
              anything. A tool would let a practitioner see, before
              materialising, which binding statements nothing will check.
              Deferred because the specification side had to land first."
  :conditions ["the prelude evaluator is merged in conjurer-mcp"
               "the server can enumerate the structural checkers it offers"]
  :cluster   :variance)

(f/candidate :intent-health-check
  :label     "A lint for specification debt in .cnj files"
  :added     "2026-10-13"
  :status    :proposed
  :scores    {:feasibility 6 :elegance 7 :containment 8 :value 8}
  :rationale "Flags decisions without a reason, :requires entries no target or
              ensure covers, and candidates never reassessed. Catches the spec
              theatre the variance surface does not: intent that is written but
              holds nothing. Builds on the health module in conjurer-mcp."
  :conditions ["check_references is in place, so coverage can be traced"
               "the thresholds (how old is a stale candidate) are decided by
                the maintainer, not inferred"]
  :cluster   :variance)

(f/candidate :divergence-probe
  :label     "Materialise one charter twice and read the differences as
              underspecified intent"
  :added     "2026-10-13"
  :status    :proposed
  :scores    {:feasibility 5 :elegance 9 :containment 7 :value 8}
  :rationale "Turns the model's variance from a risk into a detector: where two
              faithful manifestations of the same specification differ, the
              specification did not decide. Broken symmetry informs. Low
              feasibility because the generation runs on the IDE side, outside
              the deterministic tooling."
  :conditions ["two manifestations can be compared structurally, not only as
                text"]
  :cluster   :variance)

(f/candidate :sketch-mode
  :label     "An explicit exploratory mode in the language (recommendation:
              abandon)"
  :added     "2026-10-13"
  :status    :proposed
  :scores    {:feasibility 6 :elegance 4 :containment 4 :value 5}
  :rationale "The obvious way to bring exploration into the language. But allow
              and progressive refinement already leave room to explore, and a
              mode that relaxes the topology would blur exactly the distinctions
              intent topology exists to keep. Exploration belongs outside the
              charter; crystallisation (:decision/crystallisation) brings its
              results in. Recorded so the reasoning stays visible; the low
              elegance score is the finding."
  :conditions ["practitioners are observed abusing allow to mean 'not yet
                decided' at scale"]
  :cluster   :exploration)
